---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Layout title={`About | ${site.name} — Life Coach`} description="Cynthia's story: from feeling lost and hollow to reclaiming herself — through a cave, a mountain, 500 miles on foot, and 5,000 runners on a stage. This is why she coaches.">

  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="section-label">About Cynthia</p>
      <h1>I Know What It Feels Like to Lose Yourself.</h1>
      <p>And I know what it takes to find your way back. Not the polished version — the real one.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- OPENING STORY -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="about-story fade-up">
        <div class="about-story-img">
          <img src="/images/headshot-5.jpg" alt="Cynthia — Life Coach" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;" />
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="section-label">My Story</p>
          <h2>I Was a Coaching Client Before I Was a Coach.</h2>
          <p style="margin-bottom:1.2rem;">I didn't start out wanting to coach anyone. I started because I was sitting across from my own coach, not quite knowing how I'd gotten so far from myself.</p>
          <p style="margin-bottom:1.2rem;">On the outside, everything looked fine. I had a career. I had roles. I showed up, delivered, and kept moving. But underneath all of it, there was a hollowness I couldn't shake — a slow drift away from who I actually was. I was performing my life so convincingly that I'd almost convinced myself too.</p>
          <p style="margin-bottom:1.2rem;">Coaching cracked something open. It gave me back a thread — the one that leads to the real you, underneath all the roles and expectations and noise. I followed that thread. And it took me some extraordinary places.</p>
          <p>What I discovered is this: the only limits I was living inside were the ones I'd built myself. That's the thing I bring into every session — not as a theory, but as something I've lived in my body, on a stage, in a cave, on a mountain, and on a 500-mile road.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ADVENTURE STORY BLOCKS -->
  <section class="section-sm bg-card">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header center fade-up" style="margin-bottom:4rem;">
        <p class="section-label">The Journey</p>
        <h2>How I Learned to Break My Own Limits</h2>
        <p>These aren't metaphors. They're the actual moments that showed me — and still remind me — what we're all capable of.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- 1. THE STAGE -->
      <div class="story-block fade-up">
        <div class="story-block-img">
          <img src="/images/story-emcee.jpg" alt="Cynthia emceeing the Make-A-Wish Santa Run — Singapore" />
          <span class="story-tag">Make-A-Wish Santa Run · Singapore</span>
        </div>
        <div class="story-block-text">
          <span class="story-number">01 / The Stage</span>
          <h3>5,000 Runners. Two Stages. One Woman Who Almost Said No.</h3>
          <p>I was asked to emcee the Make-A-Wish Santa Run — one of Singapore's biggest charity runs, with over 5,000 runners and two stages to command simultaneously. My first instinct was to talk myself out of it.</p>
          <p>I wasn't a performer. I didn't do stages. But the part of me I'd been reclaiming in coaching knew that this exact hesitation was the thing I needed to walk through.</p>
          <p>That day, I found a version of myself I hadn't met before. Alive in front of a crowd. Completely in the moment. Not performing — actually present.</p>
          <div class="story-lesson">
            <span class="story-lesson-icon">💡</span>
            <p>The thing you're about to talk yourself out of might be exactly where you need to go.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 2. SON DOONG -->
      <div class="story-block reverse fade-up">
        <div class="story-block-img">
          <img src="/images/story-son-doong.jpg" alt="Inside Son Doong Cave, Vietnam — the largest cave in the world" />
          <span class="story-tag">Son Doong Cave · Vietnam</span>
        </div>
        <div class="story-block-text">
          <span class="story-number">02 / The Cave</span>
          <h3>The World's Largest Cave. A Posterior Annular Tear. I Went Anyway.</h3>
          <p>Son Doong in Vietnam is the largest cave in the world — so vast it contains its own weather system, its own jungle, and rivers running through the dark. Only a handful of expeditions enter each year.</p>
          <p>I had a posterior annular injury — a spinal condition that, by conventional advice, should have ruled out a 4-day jungle trek through underground rivers and rock walls. Every sensible voice said: not this one.</p>
          <p>I went anyway. Carefully, intentionally — and completely. Because I had started to understand that the edge of what's possible is almost always further than the edge of what's comfortable.</p>
          <div class="story-lesson">
            <span class="story-lesson-icon">💡</span>
            <p>"I can't do this" and "I haven't done this yet" are two very different sentences.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 3. GOKYO -->
      <div class="story-block fade-up">
        <div class="story-block-img">
          <img src="/images/story-gokyo.jpg" alt="Gokyo Valley, Nepal — suspension bridge at 5,000 metres" />
          <span class="story-tag">Gokyo Valley · Nepal · 5,000m+</span>
        </div>
        <div class="story-block-text">
          <span class="story-number">03 / The Mountain</span>
          <h3>I Fell Five Storeys in the Himalayas. I Got Back Up.</h3>
          <p>Trekking through Gokyo Valley in Nepal at over 5,000 metres, I fell — the equivalent of five storeys. The kind of fall that stops time. The kind that makes you reckon with whether you get back up or not.</p>
          <p>I got back up.</p>
          <p>At altitude, with aching legs and cold air and prayer flags snapping in the wind, something became very clear: the ground doesn't disqualify you. The fall doesn't define you. What defines you is the decision you make right after.</p>
          <div class="story-lesson">
            <span class="story-lesson-icon">💡</span>
            <p>You don't have to be unbroken to keep going. You just have to decide to.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 4. CAMINO -->
      <div class="story-block reverse fade-up">
        <div class="story-block-img">
          <img src="/images/story-camino.jpg" alt="Cynthia arriving at Santiago de Compostela — end of the Camino" />
          <span class="story-tag">Camino de Santiago · Spain</span>
        </div>
        <div class="story-block-text">
          <span class="story-number">04 / The Road</span>
          <h3>500 Miles on Foot. One Conclusion.</h3>
          <p>The Camino de Santiago is a pilgrimage — hundreds of kilometres on foot, one step at a time, with no shortcuts and no one to carry you. You walk with your thoughts. You walk through discomfort. Eventually you walk into something that feels very much like truth.</p>
          <p>What I arrived at, after all those miles, was this: the only limits that were ever real were the ones I had created myself. Not the injury. Not the mountain. Not the stage. Me.</p>
          <p>That realisation didn't make everything easy. But it made everything possible.</p>
          <div class="story-lesson">
            <span class="story-lesson-icon">💡</span>
            <p>Only I can break my own limits. That's the most liberating — and demanding — thing I know.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BRIDGE TO COACHING -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:760px;text-align:center;">
      <div class="fade-up">
        <p class="section-label">Why This Matters to You</p>
        <h2>This Is Why I Coach the Way I Do.</h2>
        <p style="margin:1rem auto 1.5rem;">I'm not sitting across from you with a clipboard and a framework. I'm sitting across from you as someone who has been lost, who has done the work, and who knows — in their body, not just their head — that what looks like a wall is usually a door.</p>
        <p style="max-width:640px;margin:0 auto;color:var(--text-light);line-height:1.8;">I work with people who feel stuck, or unsure what's next. People who've lost the thread of who they actually are — buried under roles, expectations, and the performance of being okay. People who want to reconnect with themselves and the people who matter most.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- LINKEDIN CREDIBILITY -->
  <section class="section-sm bg-card">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:760px;text-align:center;">
      <div class="fade-up">
        <p class="section-label">Verified Credibility</p>
        <h2>See the Full Picture on LinkedIn</h2>
        <p style="margin:1rem 0 2rem;">All client recommendations, work history, and ICF PCC credentials are verified and publicly visible on my LinkedIn profile.</p>
        <a href={site.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-primary" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;">
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M20.447 20.452h-3.554v-5.569c0-1.328-.027-3.037-1.852-3.037-1.853 0-2.136 1.445-2.136 2.939v5.667H9.351V9h3.414v1.561h.046c.477-.9 1.637-1.85 3.37-1.85 3.601 0 4.267 2.37 4.267 5.455v6.286zM5.337 7.433a2.062 2.062 0 01-2.063-2.065 2.064 2.064 0 112.063 2.065zm1.782 13.019H3.555V9h3.564v11.452zM22.225 0H1.771C.792 0 0 .774 0 1.729v20.542C0 23.227.792 24 1.771 24h20.451C23.2 24 24 23.227 24 22.271V1.729C24 .774 23.2 0 22.222 0h.003z"/></svg>
          View My LinkedIn Profile
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CREDENTIALS -->
  <section class="section-sm">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header center fade-up">
        <p class="section-label">Credentials</p>
        <h2>Trained, Certified & Committed</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="fade-up" style="display:flex;justify-content:center;margin:2rem 0 2.5rem;">
        <div style="text-align:center;">
          <img src="/images/pcc-badge.png" alt="ICF PCC — Professional Certified Coach" style="width:140px;height:140px;object-fit:contain;filter:drop-shadow(0 4px 12px rgba(0,0,0,.12));" />
          <p style="font-size:.8rem;color:var(--text-light);margin-top:.5rem;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;">Verified Credential</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="credentials fade-up" style="max-width:800px;margin:0 auto;">
        <div class="credential-item">
          <span class="credential-icon">🎓</span>
          <div><strong>ICF Accredited Coach — PCC Level</strong><span>International Coaching Federation</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="credential-item">
          <span class="credential-icon">🧠</span>
          <div><strong>NLP Practitioner</strong><span>Neuro-Linguistic Programming</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="credential-item">
          <span class="credential-icon">🌿</span>
          <div><strong>Mindfulness-Based Coaching</strong><span>Certified practitioner</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="credential-item">
          <span class="credential-icon">💼</span>
          <div><strong>Corporate Leadership Experience</strong><span>Strategy & Leadership roles</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="credential-item">
          <span class="credential-icon">👥</span>
          <div><strong>200+ Clients Coached</strong><span>Life coaching & mentor coaching</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="credential-item">
          <span class="credential-icon">⏱</span>
          <div><strong>600+ Hours Coached</strong><span>Logged since 2015</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="credential-item">
          <span class="credential-icon">📅</span>
          <div><strong>10+ Years Experience</strong><span>Coaching since 2015</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- VALUES -->
  <section class="section bg-card">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header center fade-up">
        <p class="section-label">What I Bring</p>
        <h2>How I Actually Work</h2>
        <p>I'm not a formula coach. I go with the flow of where you are — and I use whatever is in my toolbox to get you moving.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="values-grid fade-up">
        {[
          { icon: "💪", title: "Persistence", desc: "\"Your persistence will be what pulls you through the many obstacles in life.\" I believe this to my core — and I bring it into every session." },
          { icon: "🔍", title: "No Bullsh*t", desc: "If nobody tells you the truth and you pay me, I will tell you. From what I sense, what I see — and sometimes what you're not ready to say yet." },
          { icon: "🔥", title: "Challenged and Held", desc: "Some sessions will feel uncomfortable. I'll ask you the question you've been avoiding. But I will never leave you alone in the discomfort — I'll hold the space until you find your way through." },
          { icon: "🛡️", title: "A Genuinely Safe Space", desc: "You can be angry. You can cry. You can say the thing you've never said out loud. I will not judge you. And I'll call out the stuff that's keeping you stuck." },
          { icon: "🪞", title: "I Hold Up the Mirror", desc: "I help you see yourself more clearly — not to make you feel bad, but because there is so much more to you than your current situation." },
          { icon: "🌿", title: "You Come Back to Yourself", desc: "Lighter. Clearer. More present for the people who matter most. When you reconnect to what's core — it ripples into your relationships, your sense of who you are, and how you show up every day." },
        ].map(v => (
          <div class="value-card">
            <div class="value-icon">{v.icon}</div>
            <h4>{v.title}</h4>
            <p>{v.desc}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-banner">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="section-label">My Hand Is Waiting</p>
      <h2>Think We Might Be a Fit?</h2>
      <p class="poem-line">"I am not a little nudge. I am a force even I am afraid of."</p>
      <p>30 minutes. No pitch, no pressure. Just an honest conversation — I'll tell you straight if I think I can help, or point you to someone who can.</p>
      <div class="cta-btns">
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-white">Book My Free Call</a>
        <a href="/services" class="btn btn-outline" style="border-color:rgba(255,255,255,.3);color:#fff;">See How I Work</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>
